-- SideStreet audio manifest. The runtime audio director (Audio/Director.lua) is driven entirely
-- by this table: playlists and cue banks come from here. Generated from the owner's
-- sidestreet_manifest.json (127 entries, 2026-09-27); tools/build_audio.py would overwrite this
-- file with the stage-1 synth set, so do not run it for 0.2.0.
--
-- Core set (Media\Audio\): 10 music tracks and 12 cues, original SideStreet score rendered on the
-- owner's machine (44.1 kHz stereo Ogg Vorbis; music about -16 LUFS, cues about -14), plus the
-- three synthesized stage-1 UI cues (click, place, money).
-- Extras (Media\Audio\extras\), Sims base-game parity: 4 build, 2 buy and 3 neighbourhood tracks,
-- a loading loop on the title screen, 23 songs for the Classical, Country, Latin and Rock stations,
-- 29 piano pieces graded by skill 1-10 and 43 event stings. The extras are copied in from the
-- owner's D:\ForeverWork\SideStreetAudio\extras at install time; when a file is not there the
-- client refuses it and the director plays another variant or the core set instead.
-- Owner decision (2026-09-27): no household sound effects, ambience beds or voice files ship.
-- Calls for those names play nothing and are counted in /sidestreet diag; captions never depend
-- on audio. Some files are listed under two names (e.g. emergency/fire) so either name plays them.
--
-- Playlists ("modes"): hood, title, live, night, build, buy, create, party, venue_*, and
-- station_<id> (a stereo or radio that is on, Audio/Extras.lua) and piano_lNN (someone at the
-- piano with creativity NN).
--
-- Entry format:
--   id = {
--     file = "Interface\\AddOns\\SideStreet\\Media\\Audio\\<file>.ogg",
--     role = "music" | "cue" | "sfx" | "ambience" | "voice",
--     dur = seconds (measured duration; the director schedules by it),
--     loop = true (restarted at the end: a hard restart, not a seamless loop),
--     modes = { "hood", ... } (music only: the mode playlists the track belongs to),
--     name = "doorbell" (what callers pass to Cue/Sfx; several entries may share a name: variants),
--     title = "display title" (documentation only),
--     gain = "level notes" (documentation only: the client offers no per-sound gain),
--     source = "provenance",
--   }
